{
  "_about": [
    "The fifteen models of the study, each pinned to one commit on the Hugging Face Hub.",
    "Two Qwen ladders and one comparison family. Qwen 3 is served on the DGX-1 (v100-vllm085); Qwen 3.5 and gpt-oss are served on 80GB cards (sm80-vllm0280). Where each one runs, and with which serve file, is `deployments`. The first deployment listed is where the model is served when a command names no environment.",
    "qwen3-32b is also deployed on sm80-vllm0280 (since 2026-10-10), as a second copy of its last twelve main runs, which take about a day each on the DGX-1. Whichever copy of a run finishes first is used. Qwen 3 was checked against vLLM 0.28.0's source for it on 2026-10-10. docs/decisions/changes.md says why, and what it mixes into a Qwen 3 size trend.",
    "Checked on 2026-09-12 against the Hub API and the files at each revision, and against the source of vLLM 0.8.5.post1 and 0.28.0.",
    "`weights` is the number format the checkpoint ships in. What it is loaded as is the environment's dtype, and the two differ at the V100 site, which has no bfloat16.",
    "`parameters` is the model card's figure; `parameters_in_checkpoint` is the count of values stored in the weight files. Where a model ties its input and output embeddings -- Qwen3 0.6B, 1.7B and 4B -- the files hold that matrix twice, so the stored count is larger than the model. For Qwen 3.5 it includes the vision encoder.",
    "`thinking_prefills_open_block` is what the family's template does when a request asks for thinking: Qwen 3.5 leaves a `<think>` block open at the end of the prompt, so everything up to `</think>` in the reply is thinking; Qwen 3 prefills nothing and the model writes its own opening tag, so a reply with no tag at all is an answer. ipb.runner.response.split_reasoning needs it wherever this package does the splitting.",
    "`checkpoint_sampling_defaults` is what vLLM would apply to anything a request leaves out, were it started with its default --generation-config auto. Every serve file says vllm instead, and every request states every setting.",
    "Adding a model: one entry here, one serve file, and nothing else if its family and environment already exist. configs/README.md says what a new family or a new environment needs.",
    "Reasons for every choice: README.md in this directory, and docs/decisions/changes.md."
  ],
